/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 57 0 R
/T (STRESS AND ITS DIRECT CONTRIBUTION TO AGING Generally, stress is associated with anxiety and depression that negatively affect our mental health; however, biological sciences define it with a clear distinction between acute and chronic stress. Acute stress is the immediate, short-term anxiety you feel in everyday situations, such as running late for work. Its symptoms include anxiety, insomnia, nightmares, mood swings, and irritability. Chronic stress is a persistent and long-term condition induced by repetitive exposure to acute stress, accompanied by depression, isolation, and fatigue. Eventually, chronic stress develops into severe health problems, including digestive issues, high blood pressure, weight gain, acne, high cholesterol, stomach ulcers, and hyperthyroidism \(Srakocic, 2023\).)
/E (STRESS AND ITS DIRECT CONTRIBUTION TO AGING Generally, stress is associated with anxiety and depression that negatively affect our mental health; however, biological sciences define it with a clear distinction between acute and chronic stress. Acute stress is the immediate, short-term anxiety you feel in everyday situations, such as running late for work. Its symptoms include anxiety, insomnia, nightmares, mood swings, and irritability. Chronic stress is a persistent and long-term condition induced by repetitive exposure to acute stress, accompanied by depression, isolation, and fatigue. Eventually, chronic stress develops into severe health problems, including digestive issues, high blood pressure, weight gain, acne, high cholesterol, stomach ulcers, and hyperthyroidism \(Srakocic, 2023\).)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
