108 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 57 0 R
/T ( It has become well recognised that individuals who undergo major depressive episodes have shortened telomere length: a meta-analysis of 22 studies proves the direct proportionality of psychological stress with telomere length. Another study of healthy women who underwent chronic stress showed reduced telomere length but high urinary cortisol concentration. Even in children of 5 to 6 years of age, cortisol reactivity had a negative correlation with telomere length. Furthermore, artificially administered cortisol also inhibits the telomerase enzyme, leading to underdeveloped telomeric DNA \(Steptoe et al., 2016\).)
/E ( It has become well recognised that individuals who undergo major depressive episodes have shortened telomere length: a meta-analysis of 22 studies proves the direct proportionality of psychological stress with telomere length. Another study of healthy women who underwent chronic stress showed reduced telomere length but high urinary cortisol concentration. Even in children of 5 to 6 years of age, cortisol reactivity had a negative correlation with telomere length. Furthermore, artificially administered cortisol also inhibits the telomerase enzyme, leading to underdeveloped telomeric DNA \(Steptoe et al., 2016\).)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
