/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 59 0 R
/T ( CRISPR-based gene editing can combat the effects of stress-related genes, such as the NR3C1 gene, which causes high cortisol levels. Additionally, drug repurposing or drug designing can be used to administer senolytic drugs, which kill senescent cells through apoptotic pathways. Drugs like dasatinib, quercetin, fisetin, and navitoclax kill senescent cells, therefore mitigating senescence-associated secretory phenotype \(SASP\) and reducing oxidative stress in cells. Other examples of senolytics include CAR-T cells that recognise senescent cell markers and destroy them, whereas siRNAs silence genes that keep senescent cells alive \(Kirkland and Tchkonia, 2020\).)
/E ( CRISPR-based gene editing can combat the effects of stress-related genes, such as the NR3C1 gene, which causes high cortisol levels. Additionally, drug repurposing or drug designing can be used to administer senolytic drugs, which kill senescent cells through apoptotic pathways. Drugs like dasatinib, quercetin, fisetin, and navitoclax kill senescent cells, therefore mitigating senescence-associated secretory phenotype \(SASP\) and reducing oxidative stress in cells. Other examples of senolytics include CAR-T cells that recognise senescent cell markers and destroy them, whereas siRNAs silence genes that keep senescent cells alive \(Kirkland and Tchkonia, 2020\).)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
