/Title (CELLULAR AGING AND TELOMERIC ATTRITION  Aging, a long-existing dilemma of all life around us, is the decline in physiological functionality associated with several hallmarks: greying hair, wrinkling skin, loss of muscle mass, weakening of bones, and thickening of blood vessels. Yet aging is a cellular process \(nowhere near merely physical manifestations\), occurring within cells that are just a few micrometres wide. Age is found to be accelerated by several cellular disabilities: exhaustion of ILS pathways, exhaustion of target of rapamycin, decline in sirtuin activity, mitochondrial dysfunction, excessive senescent cells, chronic inflammation, and collapse of the proteostasis mechanism \(Campisi et al., 2019\).)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 370 0 R
/Next 374 0 R
>>
endobj
